  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 314 PM CDT Tue Sep 29 2026\n\nZonal flow will prevail through Wednesday with continued above\naverage high temperatures ranging from the mid 60s F in the\nnorth to mid 70s F in the south. Surface low pressure over\nCanada will move into the Hudson Bay region Wednesday bringing\nin high pressure and cooler temperatures behind it by Thursday\nmorning. From Thursday through the weekend, seasonable \ntemperatures with highs in the mid 50s to low 60s F and lows in \nthe mid 30s to mid 40s F are expected.\n\nThe next chance for precipitation is Saturday as a 500 mb wave\nfrom Montana moves southeast. Atmospheric lift and southerly\nwinds advecting in moisture will be enough to bring 20-50%\nprecipitation chances with the highest chances being in\nNorthwest Minnesota. This event is expected to be minor with a\n10-40% chance of getting greater than 0.25 inches of rain. High\npressure moving in behind the Saturday system is expected to\nbring cooler overnight lows Sunday and Monday with temperatures\nin the 30s F. Monday morning looks the coolest, though the\nchance for a freeze remains low (0-30%) for much of region. \n\nAs we move into next week, especially Tuesday, ensemble systems\nare generally indicating that above average heights will return\nto the region bringing above average temperatures. From the Red\nRiver Valley and west, there is a 30-60% chance of seeing a \nhigh temperature of 70 F or greater Tuesday. Dry conditions are \nalso favored for next week.",
